<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mandinka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mandinka are a West African people of the Mande group, living mainly in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-gambia">Gambia</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundiata-keita">Sundiata Keita</a>, they founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>. Mandinka expansion westward also produced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu Empire</a>, and Mandinka communities interacted with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jolof-empire">Jolof Empire</a>.</p></div>
